questions.question_text:
$PQRS$ is a parallelogram with $\overrightarrow{PQ}=\underset{\sim}{c}$ and $\overrightarrow{PS}=\underset{\sim}{d}$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{QS}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4.4,2.2);
\coordinate (S) at (1.2,2.2);
\draw[->,thick] (P) -- (Q) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{c}$};
\draw[->,thick] (P) -- (S) node[midway,left] {$\underset{\sim}{d}$};
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\draw (R) -- (S);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above left] at (S) {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $\overrightarrow{OX}=\underset{\sim}{m}$, $\overrightarrow{OY}=\underset{\sim}{n}$ and $M$ is the midpoint of $XY$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{MY}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (X) at (3.5,0.3);
\coordinate (Y) at (0.9,2.9);
\coordinate (M) at ($(X)!0.5!(Y)$);
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (X) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{m}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (Y) node[midway,left] {$\underset{\sim}{n}$};
\draw (X) -- (Y);
\fill (M) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[right] at (X) {$X$};
\node[above] at (Y) {$Y$};
\node[above right] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $\overrightarrow{OA}=\underset{\sim}{s}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}=\underset{\sim}{t}$.
The point $P$ lies on $AB$ with $AP:PB=2:3$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{OP}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (3.5,0.4);
\coordinate (B) at (1.0,3.0);
\coordinate (P) at ($(A)!0.4!(B)$);
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{s}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (B) node[midway,left] {$\underset{\sim}{t}$};
\draw (A) -- (B);
\fill (P) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the quadrilateral $KLMN$, $\overrightarrow{KL}=\underset{\sim}{j}$, $\overrightarrow{ML}=\underset{\sim}{k}$ and $\overrightarrow{MN}=\underset{\sim}{l}$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{KN}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (K) at (0,0);
\coordinate (L) at (3.0,-0.6);
\coordinate (M) at (4.4,1.8);
\coordinate (N) at (1.2,2.6);
\draw[->,thick] (K) -- (L) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{j}$};
\draw[->,thick] (M) -- (L) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{k}$};
\draw[->,thick] (M) -- (N) node[midway,above] {$\underset{\sim}{l}$};
\draw (K) -- (N);
\node[left] at (K) {$K$};
\node[below] at (L) {$L$};
\node[right] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above left] at (N) {$N$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$W$, $X$, $Y$ and $Z$ are the points shown.
Which single vector equals $\overrightarrow{XY}-\overrightarrow{ZY}+\overrightarrow{ZW}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.1]
\coordinate (X) at (0,0.6);
\coordinate (Y) at (2.4,2.6);
\coordinate (Z) at (4.0,0.6);
\coordinate (W) at (5.6,2.6);
\draw[->,thick] (X) -- (Y);
\draw[->,thick] (Z) -- (Y);
\draw[->,thick] (Z) -- (W);
\node[left] at (X) {$X$};
\node[above] at (Y) {$Y$};
\node[below] at (Z) {$Z$};
\node[right] at (W) {$W$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In triangle $PQR$, $\overrightarrow{PQ}=4\underset{\sim}{u}$ and $\overrightarrow{PR}=4\underset{\sim}{w}$.
$M$ is the midpoint of $PQ$ and $N$ is the midpoint of $PR$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{MN}$?
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.6,0.4);
\coordinate (R) at (1.0,3.0);
\coordinate (M) at ($(P)!0.5!(Q)$);
\coordinate (N) at ($(P)!0.5!(R)$);
\draw[->,thick] (P) -- (Q) node[midway,below] {$4\underset{\sim}{u}$};
\draw[->,thick] (P) -- (R) node[midway,left] {$4\underset{\sim}{w}$};
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\draw[dashed] (M) -- (N);
\fill (M) circle (2pt);
\fill (N) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above] at (M) {$M$};
\node[right] at (N) {$N$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

$ABCD$ is a parallelogram with $\overrightarrow{AB}=\underset{\sim}{g}$ and $\overrightarrow{BC}=\underset{\sim}{h}$.
The point $E$ lies on the diagonal $AC$ with $AE:EC=1:4$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{AE}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,2.2);
\coordinate (D) at (1.2,2.2);
\coordinate (E) at ($(A)!0.2!(C)$);
\draw[->,thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{g}$};
\draw[->,thick] (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{h}$};
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\fill (E) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (E) {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the quadrilateral $ABCD$, $\overrightarrow{AB}=\underset{\sim}{p}$, $\overrightarrow{BC}=\underset{\sim}{q}$ and $\overrightarrow{CD}=\underset{\sim}{r}$.
$M$ is the midpoint of $AD$.
Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{BM}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0.4);
\coordinate (B) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.6,2.0);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,3.2);
\coordinate (M) at ($(A)!0.5!(D)$);
\draw[->,thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{p}$};
\draw[->,thick] (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{q}$};
\draw[->,thick] (C) -- (D) node[midway,above right] {$\underset{\sim}{r}$};
\draw (D) -- (A);
\fill (M) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (D) {$D$};
\node[left] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
